{"id":"h19t4","name":"Ledger with Holds and Scheduled Transfers","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["queries"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Implement the ledger of a payment app. Every query starts with a timestamp (digits); queries are sorted by timestamp. Process them in order and return one string per query. All amounts are integers.</p>\n<p>An account has a <b>balance</b> and can have <b>holds</b> (money reserved for a card payment). A hold created at time <code>t</code> with a <code>ttl</code> is active while the current time is lower than <code>t + ttl</code>, and stops being active from <code>t + ttl</code> on. The <b>available</b> amount of an account at a time is its balance minus its active holds.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>[t, \"OPEN\", acc]</code>: <code>\"true\"</code>, or <code>\"false\"</code> if the account exists.</li>\n<li><code>[t, \"DEPOSIT\", acc, amount]</code>: adds to the balance; returns the available amount.</li>\n<li><code>[t, \"HOLD\", acc, hold_id, amount, ttl]</code>: creates a hold if the available amount is at least <code>amount</code> and <code>hold_id</code> was never used; returns the available amount after it.</li>\n<li><code>[t, \"CAPTURE\", hold_id]</code>: if the hold is still active, the money leaves the account (the balance decreases and the hold disappears): <code>\"true\"</code>; else <code>\"false\"</code>.</li>\n<li><code>[t, \"SCHEDULE\", from, to, amount, delay]</code>: plans a transfer for the time <code>t + delay</code> and returns its id: <code>\"transfer1\"</code> for the first scheduled transfer of the whole ledger, then <code>\"transfer2\"</code>, and so on. Refused with <code>\"\"</code> if an account is unknown or if <code>from</code> equals <code>to</code> (no id is used).</li>\n<li><code>[t, \"CANCEL\", transfer_id]</code>: <code>\"true\"</code> if the transfer is still planned (it is removed), else <code>\"false\"</code>.</li>\n<li><code>[t, \"TOP\", n]</code>: the <code>n</code> accounts with the highest total of money sent (captured holds and executed transfers), as <code>\"acc(total)\"</code> items joined with <code>\",\"</code>, highest first, then by account name. All accounts are ranked, even with a total of 0.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A query on an unknown account or hold, and a refused <code>HOLD</code>, returns <code>\"\"</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Before</b> processing a query at time <code>t</code>, execute every planned transfer whose time is at most <code>t</code>, in order of their time, then id number. A transfer is executed if the available amount of the sender <b>at the transfer's time</b> is at least the amount: the money moves from one balance to the other. Otherwise it fails and is dropped.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>queries = [[\"1\", \"OPEN\", \"ana\"], [\"1\", \"OPEN\", \"ben\"], [\"2\", \"DEPOSIT\", \"ana\", \"100\"], [\"3\", \"HOLD\", \"ana\", \"h1\", \"70\", \"10\"], [\"4\", \"SCHEDULE\", \"ana\", \"ben\", \"50\", \"5\"], [\"5\", \"SCHEDULE\", \"ana\", \"ben\", \"30\", \"11\"], [\"8\", \"HOLD\", \"ana\", \"h2\", \"40\", \"5\"], [\"12\", \"CAPTURE\", \"h1\"], [\"13\", \"TOP\", \"2\"], [\"16\", \"DEPOSIT\", \"ben\", \"0\"], [\"17\", \"CAPTURE\", \"h2\"], [\"17\", \"TOP\", \"5\"]]</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[\"true\", \"true\", \"100\", \"30\", \"transfer1\", \"transfer2\", \"\", \"true\", \"ana(70),ben(0)\", \"30\", \"false\", \"ana(100),ben(0)\"]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.array.string queries<br><b>[output]</b> array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(queries):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["système à plusieurs commandes","réservations qui expirent","virements planifiés","traitement des échéances avant chaque requête","classement"],"minutes":40,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solution(queries)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Ici, la valeur attendue est une liste : compare ce que tu renvoies à « Expected return value » dans les résultats.</li><li>La comparaison est exacte (même type, mêmes valeurs, même ordre dans une liste), sauf les nombres décimaux, comparés à 0,000001 près.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 10 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"queries":[["1","OPEN","ana"],["1","OPEN","ben"],["2","DEPOSIT","ana","100"],["3","HOLD","ana","h1","70","10"],["4","SCHEDULE","ana","ben","50","5"],["5","SCHEDULE","ana","ben","30","11"],["8","HOLD","ana","h2","40","5"],["12","CAPTURE","h1"],["13","TOP","2"],["16","DEPOSIT","ben","0"],["17","CAPTURE","h2"],["17","TOP","5"]]},"expected":{"value":["true","true","100","30","transfer1","transfer2","","true","ana(70),ben(0)","30","false","ana(100),ben(0)"]}},{"input":{"queries":[["0","OPEN","a"],["0","OPEN","b"],["0","DEPOSIT","a","10"],["0","SCHEDULE","a","b","10","3"],["1","SCHEDULE","a","b","10","2"],["2","CANCEL","transfer1"],["2","CANCEL","transfer1"],["3","SCHEDULE","a","a","1","1"],["3","HOLD","zz","h","1","1"],["3","TOP","1"],["4","DEPOSIT","a","5"],["4","HOLD","b","h9","10","1"],["5","HOLD","b","h9","1","1"],["5","CAPTURE","h9"]]},"expected":{"value":["true","true","10","transfer1","transfer2","true","false","","","a(10)","5","0","","false"]}}],"hidden_n":10,"hidden":"","solution":""}